      <description>FasterXML jackson-databind before 2.7.9.3, 2.8.x before 2.8.11.1 and 2.9.x before 2.9.5 allows unauthenticated remote code execution because of an incomplete fix for the CVE-2017-7525 deserialization flaw.</description>
      <detail>This vulnerability impacts the jackson-databind component. When the default typing feature is enabled (either globally or for a specific type) it is possible for a user to provide an Object that can be deserialized into a BadAttributeValueExpException object.</detail>
      <recommendation>Upgrade to version 2.9.5 or later</recommendation>
